      <workList xml:id="workDesc_efb4ebac">
         <work xml:id="work_id470f0daf">
            <identifier label="SchW" xml:id="identifier_8ad45ab3">A1:008</identifier>
            <title xml:id="title_id25289d2a" xml:lang="it">Concerto in D</title>
            <contributor xml:id="respStmt_9a2ea940">
               <persName role="composer" xml:id="persName_idd4175e94">Johann Adolph Scheibe</persName>
            </contributor>
            <history xml:id="history_id36ea2d3a">
               <p xml:id="idm70">The present work for flute and strings has apparently been lost. It is listed in the catalogue of the Fürstlich zu Bentheim-Tecklenburgische Musikbibliothek, with incipit. <persName xml:id="idm71" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" auth="VIAF" role="">Count Moritz Casimir I</persName>, who reigned 1710–68, played both the flute and cello in the daily court concerts which took place before dinner ('Tafel'). The work must have been acquired before 1750 – perhaps through a contact to the collegium musicum in Leipzig – when the thematic catalogue was begun by <persName xml:id="idm72" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" auth="VIAF" role="">Johann Martin Doemming</persName> in November that year. The collection includes manuscripts of works by <persName xml:id="idm73" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" auth="VIAF" role="">Georg Philipp Telemann</persName>, the <persName xml:id="idm74" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" auth="VIAF" role="">Graun</persName> brothers (Carl Heinrich and Johann Gottlieb) and <persName xml:id="idm75" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" auth="VIAF" role="">Johan Joachim Agrell</persName>, among others. It is also possible that the transcript was obtained directly from Scheibe after he started his employment as Kapellmeister at the Danish court in 1740.</p>
            </history>
            <langUsage xml:id="langUsage_cc9e0cfe">
               <language xml:id="it">Italian</language>
               <language xml:id="en">English</language>
            </langUsage>
